      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Chat with the knowledge base\nA chat message goes to the AI Agent, which uses Gemini to respond. \nThe agent can query the Supabase vector store for relevant information. \nNo memory connection is shown.",
        "height": 448,
        "width": 1552,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "9c70102e-004b-4f8c-9940-dad133b6069b",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1424,
        -368
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Ingest new documents\nWhen a file is created in the Google Drive folder \"Knowledge Base Document\" (checked every minute), \nit is downloaded, split into a document, embedded with Google Gemini, \nand stored in the Supabase \"documents\" vector table. \nThe Drive file ID is saved as metadata (file_id).",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 1552,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "258bb51c-671f-46bb-9e62-a25173b4b0ae",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1184,
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Re-index updated documents\nWhen a file in the same Drive folder is updated, its old vectors are deleted from Supabase (matched by file_id metadata). \nThe new version is then downloaded, embedded with Gemini, and re-inserted, so answers never use stale content.",
        "height": 432,
        "width": 1568,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "8002ffe5-5802-4697-a907-3f5043e301dd",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1152,
        544
      ]
    }
